    "goal": "Determine the wall shear stress and pressure drop experienced by endothelium in a 400x100 µm rectangular channel perfused at 2 µL/min with medium viscosity 1e-3 Pa·s over a 20 mm length.",
    "rationale": "This is a pure flow-mechanics calculation for a perfused microchannel. The channel is 400 µm wide, 100 µm high, 20 mm long, perfused at 2 µL/min per channel with water-like culture medium (viscosity 1e-3 Pa·s, density 1000 kg/m³). The wall shear stress and pressure drop are computed from the standard wide-rectangular-channel laminar-flow relations. The resulting shear (≈0.05 Pa) falls in the hepatic sinusoidal range (0.05-0.15 Pa) and at the low end of the microvascular endothelial range (0.1-1 Pa); the pressure drop is modest and well within syringe-pump capability.",
